---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import diagramLight from '../../../docs/assets/how-it-works.svg';
import diagramDark from '../../../docs/assets/how-it-works-dark.svg';
import demo from '../../../docs/assets/compaction.mp4';

// Home page copy is drawn from the facts in the repo README; keep the two in step.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const repo = 'https://github.com/lemun/kitzur';
const tagline =
  'A zero-dependency local proxy between your coding agent and its model server. It compacts each request to fit the window your model actually serves. No second LLM is called to do it.';

// No ratings, reviews or offers: the README cites none.
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'Kitzur',
  description:
    'Zero-dependency context compaction proxy for coding agents using local LLMs. Keep coding in the context window your local model actually serves.',
  url: new URL(`${base}/`, Astro.site).href,
  applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Windows, macOS, Linux',
  softwareRequirements: 'Node.js 22+',
  license: `${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`,
  downloadUrl: repo,
};

const fromSource = `git clone https://github.com/lemun/kitzur.git
cd kitzur
npm ci
npm run build
node dist/src/cli.js config init --preset 32k --out ~/.config/kitzur/kitzur.jsonc \\
  --upstream http://127.0.0.1:8000 --tokenizer /path/to/tokenizer.json
node dist/src/cli.js serve --config ~/.config/kitzur/kitzur.jsonc`;

const globalCommand = `npm pack                        # after npm run build; writes kitzur-<version>.tgz
npm install -g ./kitzur-*.tgz
kitzur version`;
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Kitzur',
		description: 'Keep coding in the context window your local model actually serves.',
		template: 'splash',
		head: [{ tag: 'script', attrs: { type: 'application/ld+json' }, content: JSON.stringify(jsonLd) }],
		hero: {
			title: 'Keep coding in the context window your local model actually serves',
			tagline,
			actions: [
				{ text: 'Quick start', link: `${base}/docs/quick-start/`, icon: 'right-arrow' },
				{ text: 'View on GitHub', link: repo, variant: 'minimal', icon: 'external' },
			],
		},
	}}
>
	<h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
	<p>
		Kitzur shrinks each request before it reaches your model: older history becomes a structured,
		mechanical summary of instructions, decisions and open work, recent messages stay intact, and
		oversized tool output is trimmed.
	</p>
	<img
		class="kz-diagram dark:sl-hidden"
		src={diagramLight.src}
		width={diagramLight.width}
		height={diagramLight.height}
		alt="Diagram: a coding agent sends a long context to the Kitzur proxy, which extracts a structured summary, keeps recent work and trims oversized outputs, then forwards a smaller request to the model server."
	/>
	<img
		class="kz-diagram light:sl-hidden"
		src={diagramDark.src}
		width={diagramDark.width}
		height={diagramDark.height}
		alt="Diagram: a coding agent sends a long context to the Kitzur proxy, which extracts a structured summary, keeps recent work and trims oversized outputs, then forwards a smaller request to the model server."
	/>

	<h2 id="benefits">Why use it</h2>
	<div class="kz-cards">
		<section>
			<h3>Fits the served window</h3>
			<p>
				Compacts before the request overflows, keeps recent tool calls paired with their results, and
				retries recognized overflows with smaller requests.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>No second model</h3>
			<p>
				Deterministic extraction and trimming run locally with zero runtime dependencies. Transcript
				files are left unchanged.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h3>You can see it work</h3>
			<p>
				Every response carries <code>x-kitzur-action</code> and <code>x-kitzur-tokens</code>;
				<code>kitzur status</code> shows recent requests. Default logs omit message content.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<h2 id="demo">Demo</h2>
	<figure class="kz-demo">
		<video src={demo} controls muted playsinline preload="metadata">
			<a href={demo}>Watch the compaction demo (MP4)</a>
		</video>
		<figcaption>
			Scripted demo against a stub upstream, not a model. A session grows past a 32k window through
			Kitzur; the proxy reports passthrough, compact and reuse actions, and <code>kitzur status</code>
			shows the last compaction from 52,147 to 6,432 tokens.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>

	<h2 id="evidence">Evidence</h2>
	<aside class="kz-evidence">
		<p>
			<strong>46/46 steps completed through Kitzur · 7/7 planted facts retained · No client errors.</strong>
			In a 46-step simulated browser session with a 100,000-token window and 32,000 tokens reserved
			for output, the direct client was rejected at step 11. Kitzur processed 31.4% fewer prompt
			tokens than the offline OpenCode compaction simulation.
		</p>
		<p><strong>Limits.</strong></p>
		<ul>
			<li>These are measured mock-server requests, not a live model solving a task.</li>
			<li>Fact retention checks marker presence, not model comprehension.</li>
			<li>
				They establish compaction behavior, not inference speed, billing savings or real-model task
				quality; live-model coding validation is pending.
			</li>
			<li>Summaries are mechanical and budget-bounded: under pressure, facts and user text can be shortened.</li>
		</ul>
		<p><a href={`${base}/docs/benchmarks/`}>Benchmark methodology</a></p>
	</aside>

	<h2 id="compatibility">Compatibility</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr><th>HTTP format</th><th>Clients</th><th>Intended environment</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>OpenAI Chat Completions only</td>
				<td>OpenCode example; any compatible client</td>
				<td>Local or intranet model with a known served window</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>
		Anthropic Messages and OpenAI Responses are unsupported. Presets cover 32k, 64k, 100k and 128k
		windows. Requires Node.js 22+.
	</p>

	<h2 id="install">Install</h2>
	<h3>From source</h3>
	<Code code={fromSource} lang="sh" />
	<h3>As a <code>kitzur</code> command</h3>
	<Code code={globalCommand} lang="sh" />
	<h3>Offline or as a service</h3>
	<p>
		Build the offline bundle with <code>scripts/pack-offline.sh</code>, or run Kitzur as a
		Windows, macOS or Linux service: see <a href={`${base}/docs/deployment/`}>deployment</a>. Then
		<a href={`${base}/docs/quick-start/`}>point your agent at the proxy</a>.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.kz-diagram {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: var(--kz-radius);
	}
	.kz-cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.kz-cards section,
	.kz-evidence {
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: var(--kz-radius);
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
	}
	.kz-cards section > :first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.kz-demo video {
		width: 100%;
		border-radius: var(--kz-radius);
	}
	.kz-demo figcaption {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
</style>
